  "worked_solution": "Let $x$ be the baseline enrollment.\n\nWe're told that enrollment grew to $180%$ of the baseline. Thus, the new enrollment is $1.8x.$\n\nWe are also told that of those enrolled, $15%$ chose yoga. So, the number of people who chose yoga is\n\n$$\n0.15(1.8x)=0.27x.\n$$\n\nThe expression $0.27x$ represents $27%$ of $x.$ Therefore, $27%$ of the baseline chose yoga.",
